#: admin/admin-page.php:1221
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, you’ll learn how to display Dynamic AJAX Product Filters using the Gutenberg (Block) Editor in WooCommerce.\n"
"\n"
"We’ll cover both methods:\n"
"-Using the Widget (Block-based Widgets screen)\n"
"-Using the Page Editor (Gutenberg blocks)\n"
"This allows you to easily add product filters to shop pages, archive pages, or custom layouts without any coding."
msgstr ""

#: admin/admin-page.php:1234
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, you’ll learn how to display Dynamic AJAX Product Filters in Divi using the shortcode method for WooCommerce.\n"
"If you’re using the Divi theme or Divi Builder, this video will show you how to easily insert product filters anywhere on your site without coding. Using shortcodes ensures full compatibility and flexible placement within Divi layouts."
msgstr ""

#: admin/admin-page.php:1243
msgid ""
"Learn how to configure mobile-responsive filters using Dynamic AJAX Product Filters for WooCommerce to ensure a smooth shopping experience on all devices.\n"
"This tutorial focuses on optimizing filters for mobile users without compromising performance or design."
msgstr ""

#: admin/admin-page.php:1252
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, you’ll learn how to display active filter chips (selected filters) using Dynamic AJAX Product Filters for WooCommerce across multiple builders and methods.\n"
"We’ll show you how to display the active filters widget."
msgstr ""

#: admin/admin-page.php:1261
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, you’ll learn how to display a Single Button Style Product Filter using Dynamic AJAX Product Filters for WooCommerce with multiple methods.\n"
"We’ll show how to add and use the single button filter with Widget,\n"
"Elementor, Gutenberg Shortcode. Single button style filters are perfect for minimal UI designs, mobile-friendly layouts, and stores that want a clean, distraction-free filtering experience."
msgstr ""

